,title,link,text,language,family
0,Malankuravan language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malankuravan_language,"Malankuravan (Mala Koravan, Malakkuravan, IPA: [mɐlɐŋɡurɐʋɐn]) is an unclassified Dravidian language of southern India, on the southern border of Kerala and Tamil Nadu.",Malankuravan,Dravidian
1,Dravidian peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dravidian_peoples,"Carnatic music originated in the Dravidian region. With the growing influence of Persian and Sufi music on Indian music, a clear distinction in style appeared from the 12th century onwards.",Malankuravan,Dravidian
2,Malankuravan language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/malankuravan_language,"The Malankuravan language, spoken by the Malankuravan (or Mala Kuravan) tribal community along the southern Kerala-Tamil Nadu border, traces its roots to the broader Dravidian language family, with its development intertwined with the evolution of regional Dravidian varieties in tribal settings.",Malankuravan,Dravidian
